{"name":"Indifferent","hex":"#9892b8","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"indifferent","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Ambivalent; unconcerned; uninterested, apathetic.","Indicating or reflecting a lack of concern or care."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who is indifferent or apathetic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/indifferent"}],"entries":[{"title":"Apathy","blocks":[{"text":"Apathy, also referred to as indifference, is a lack of feeling, emotion, interest, and/or concern about something. It is a state of indifference, and/or the suppression of emotions such as concern, excitement, motivation, or passion. An apathetic individual has an absence of interest in or concern about emotional, social, spiritual, philosophical, virtual, or physical life and the world. Apathy can also be defined as a person's lack of goal orientation. Apathy falls in the less extreme spectrum of diminished motivation, with abulia in the middle and akinetic mutism being more extreme than both apathy and abulia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Challenge_vs_skill.svg/330px-Challenge_vs_skill.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apathy","wikidata":"Q309406"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"indifferent":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5a/En-us-indifferent.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/5/5a/En-us-indifferent.ogg/En-us-indifferent.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Grey Bushchat in Sillery Gaon March 2025 by Tisha Mukherjee 01","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Grey_Bushchat_in_Sillery_Gaon_March_2025_by_Tisha_Mukherjee_01.jpg/500px-Grey_Bushchat_in_Sillery_Gaon_March_2025_by_Tisha_Mukherjee_01.jpg","ra